From 142553d6f0ba92d8bb107e282df8a50be649df4f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:15:59 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(kanban): each hub final-gate refusal branch has its own
 reason [daveey]

Problem: hub 2026-11-13 02:00-04:30Z, hub-local claims (t_01a19400313cfbda, t_01a184cee94603eb, t_7d17e13d)
took a Board grant, released it unused ~5 s later, and the skip event and queue line said only
`claim_deferred (hub_cpu_unknown)` while the advisory sample was fresh at ~25 % (limit 50 %). Five different
final-gate branches returned that one code, so the event could not say which fired.

Five whys (card t_01a1d2d70c134f11, comment 58821): the branch that fired was the hold overrun. py-spy on the hub
gateway put 14.0 s of 16.9 s of claim_transaction in the census's per-column `PRAGMA table_info` reads, each row step
re-acquiring the GIL behind busy threads, plus the ~1 s sample under the lock. Main has since fixed that root
(cc9d41d953 one-statement census; 6bd4b97b00f the gate reads the sampler's sample instead of sampling under the
lock; the overrun is `hub_admission_overrun`). Since 05:01Z hub claims admit again. The remaining final-gate
branches still share `hub_cpu_unknown`.

Fix (the CPU limit, the cap and the hold bound are unchanged):
- each remaining final-gate branch gets its own reason in the skip event / queue line, and the stage and hold_ms
  stay in the refusal log: hub_cpu_limit_unknown (root limit unreadable/invalid), hub_cpu_gate_expired (deadline
  passed before the census), hub_cpu_sample_stale (sampler sample missing/stale/malformed at the lock),
  hub_cpu_gate_expired_counting (deadline passed during the census), plus main's hub_admission_overrun. The
  lock-free advisory keeps hub_cpu_unknown for its own sample. The codes are added to kanban_queue_reason.CODES.
- machine_metrics.table_columns reads a table's columns in ONE row (pragma_table_info + group_concat). The census's
  legacy fallback, board_pools and origin_key use it on the claim connection under admission.lock.

Tests: test_kanban_hub_gate_convoy.py (reasons distinct, in the queue line and in CODES; census steps bounded;
table_columns is one row; pool/origin lookups use it), test_hub_cpu_gate_contention.py (each branch asserts its
reason and stage, including the new lease_expired_after_census case), test_kanban_hub_admission{,_sampler_read}.py.
RED on main 5d855bcb37e: both new-reason files fail at collection and the sampler re-check refuses as
hub_cpu_unknown. GREEN: 16 admission/metrics/queue files, 525 passed.
